<title>USA: Fed Realty buys stake in shopping center.</title>
<headline>Fed Realty buys stake in shopping center.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Realty Investment Trust said on Friday it has acquired a controlling interest in a limited liability company formed to own Escondido Promenade shopping center in California.</p>
<p>The property is valued at $23.4 million and is subject to $9.4 million of existing financing in the form of long-term, tax-free bonds.</p>
<p>Federal Realty invested $14 million in the LLC on which it is projected to receive a 12 percent preferred return, the company said. The seller will continue to manage and lease the center, Federal Realty said.</p>
